================================================================================
 2. DFHACK
================================================================================

DFHack is distributed under the zlib licence, with some MIT- and BSD-licensed
components. The complete licence text, including every third-party component
(clsocket, dirent, JSON.lua, jsoncpp, libexpat, libzip, linenoise, Lua, luacov,
luafilesystem, lua-profiler, protobuf, tinythread, tinyxml, UTF-8-decoder,
xlsxio and alt-getopt), is reproduced in full in:

    game/hack/LICENSE.rst

Copyright (c) 2009-2012, Petr Mrazek and the DFHack contributors.

The Dreamfort blueprint set that Antfarm's guided build drives ships with
DFHack, in game/blueprints/library/dreamfort.csv, and is by Mike Stewart
("Wittzeng"). The quickfort blueprint system it uses is by Joel Meador and the
DFHack team.


================================================================================
 3. DF-AI -- Ben Lubar
================================================================================

Antfarm's modal watchdog (game/hack/scripts/antfarm_ui.lua) ports solutions from
df-ai: the viewscreen-to-interface-key table, is_dwarfmode_viewscreen, the
announcement-type pause classification, the stuck-pause backstop and the
post-unpause camera restore. df-ai is at https://github.com/BenLubar/df-ai and
is by Ben Lubar, originally written in Ruby by Yoann Guillot (jjyg).

df-ai is distributed under the zlib licence:

